# KINETIC ENGINE CONFIGURATION: CITY-FIRST SPOKE EXPANSION
# Target: Oregon Exterior Experts CMS (Supabase)
# Inherits: blog-template.mdc (Founder voice, Topic Clusters, Oregon Reality filters, Linking Logic, Technical Constraints, Execution Order)
# Depends on: Phase 1 completion (7 pillars + 21 spokes delivered via waves 001–007, zero failures)

## [PROCEDURAL TASK]
**Phase 2: Portland — Full Cluster Coverage**

Generate 3–4 Spoke Posts per cluster (21–28 total) targeting Portland, OR. All 7 clusters receive city-specific spoke content. Every post in this phase has `target_city: "Portland"`.

**No new pillar posts.** The 7 Phase 1 pillars remain the permanent hubs. Each Phase 2 spoke links back to its Phase 1 pillar (via `parent_post`) and cross-links to both Phase 1 and Phase 2 sibling spokes.

The goal is to prove full geographic dominance for a single city across every topic cluster before expanding to additional cities in later phases.

## [FILE OUTPUT PROTOCOL]
Before generating any posts, read and follow: @.cursor/rules/blog-output-protocol.mdc

All generated posts MUST:
- Be routed to the correct cluster folder (cluster-1-moss-algae-prevention through cluster-7-home-exterior-health)
- Be placed in the `phase2/` subfolder within each cluster
- Follow naming convention: `spoke-{title-slug}.md` (slug derived from `h1_title`, see output protocol)
- Use the cluster mapping and file routing rules defined in the output protocol
- No `pillar-` files are generated in Phase 2

## [BATCH 0: CONTENT MANIFEST]
The Content Manifest schema template is at `blog/data/manifest.json`.
Phase 1 completed manifest (for cross-phase reference) is at `blog/data/completed/phase1.json`.

Read the manifest JSON file. The following fields are pre-filled and locked — do NOT modify them:
`cluster`, `post_type` (always `"spoke"`), `primary_keyword`, `h1_title`, `intent`, `parent_post`, `sibling_posts`, `target_city` (always `"Portland"`)

Complete ONLY fields set to `null`:
- `slug` — derive from `primary_keyword` + `"Portland"`
- `one_sentence_summary` — write using the `primary_keyword` in the Founder voice, shaped by the `intent` classification
- `target_neighborhood` — read `blog/data/neighborhood-matrix.json`, select a neighborhood from the Portland array. Distribute neighborhoods across posts so no two posts in the same cluster share the same neighborhood. Also avoid neighborhoods already used by Phase 1 Portland-targeted posts (check `blog/data/completed/phase1.json`).
- `target_landmark` — read `blog/data/landmark-matrix.json`, select a landmark from the Portland array. Choose a landmark geographically near the chosen `target_neighborhood`. Distribute landmarks across posts so no two posts in the same cluster share the same landmark. Also avoid landmarks already used by Phase 1 Portland-targeted posts.

Do NOT modify any pre-filled fields. Write the completed manifest to `blog/data/completed/phase2.json` before proceeding to Batch 1.

## [BATCH 1: SPOKE POSTS]
Generate the Phase 2 Spoke Posts (3–4 per cluster) using the completed Content Manifest as a reference for all parent and sibling links.

Format:
- H1: Use `h1_title` from the manifest
- Intent: Split `intent` on ` / `. Read `blog/data/intent-matrix.json`. Apply `primary_intents[primary]` as the base, then merge any `*_override` fields from `modifiers[modifier]`. Use the resolved `tone`, `cta_placement`, `content_depth`, and `structure` to shape the post.
- Oregon Reality: Pull Portland-specific data from `blog/data/geo-reference-matrix.json` (`soil_geology`, `tree_biological_load`, `regulation`). Reference the post's `target_neighborhood` and `target_landmark` from the completed manifest.
- Body: Intro (Portland-specific problem framing) -> The Physics/Evidence -> The Code/Standard -> The Fix. Close with "The Bigger Picture" paragraph linking back to the Phase 1 pillar (via `parent_post`) and referencing sibling spokes (via `sibling_posts`).

### [CROSS-PHASE LINKING]
Phase 2 spokes exist within the Phase 1 hub-and-spoke topology. Linking rules:

- **Upward (required):** Every Phase 2 spoke links to its Phase 1 pillar via `parent_post`. Use the standard "The Bigger Picture" closing format.
- **Lateral (required):** `sibling_posts` may include both Phase 1 spoke keywords and Phase 2 spoke keywords. Link to all siblings listed in the manifest.
- **Anchor text:** Follow the layered-defense keyword style defined in @.cursor/rules/blog-template.mdc — e.g., "Portland's first line of gutter defense," "the drainage layer protecting your Portland foundation."